Subject: AOT: a call to a compiled callee with fewer arguments than it declares enters the compiled body from the interpreter's call path

What this does
  - `aot_call_light_impl` (the interpreter's call of a callee that has a compiled body) used to refuse a call whose argument count `na` was below the callee's declared count (`na < cb->arg_count`), which sent it through `regvm_t_call_slow`, `JS_CallInternal`, `js_regvm_execute` and the compiled entry. It now extends the window with undefined in a copy of up to 16 declared arguments and enters the compiled body with that copy and the real `na` (the callee's `arguments` and `.length` still see `na`; a callee declaring more than 16 arguments keeps the old path).

Why we need it
  R5 (aot_bench call.arity 0.77x of the interpreter): a compiled caller leaves at a call that supplies fewer arguments than the callee declares, the rest of the activation runs in the interpreter, and every such call into the compiled callee paid the full C-entry path. kit arityfew: 1709 -> 1604 Minstr (interpreter 1351).

Soundness
  The compiled bodies read the declared arguments directly from the window; the copy gives them the undefined values the interpreter's own padding gives a short call, and it lives on the C stack for the duration of the call (the callee finishes before the function returns; an `arguments` object copies).
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -70038 +70038 @@
-    if (cb->func_kind != JS_FUNC_NORMAL || na < cb->arg_count)
+    if (cb->func_kind != JS_FUNC_NORMAL)
@@ -70039,0 +70040,14 @@
+    /* A call with fewer arguments than the callee declares: the compiled body reads the declared ones, so the window is
+       extended with undefined in a copy (the callee's `arguments` and `.length` still see `na`). Without this the call took
+       JS_CallInternal, js_regvm_execute and the compiled entry: 1.3x the cost of the interpreter's own call (aot_bench call.arity). */
+    JSValue padded[16];
+    if (unlikely(na < cb->arg_count)) {
+        int i;
+        if (cb->arg_count > 16)
+            return 0;
+        for (i = 0; i < na; i++)
+            padded[i] = argv[i];
+        for (; i < cb->arg_count; i++)
+            padded[i] = JS_UNDEFINED;
+        argv = padded;
+    }
